# ── Counterfactual: one unguarded credential route ADDED ─────────────────────
# A different class from its siblings: the constitution PLUS a line, not minus
# one. The added rule is the one somebody might someday write — a pen route
# that forgets ~match(·, CarriedVoid) and ~broken — and this fixture is what
# the world looks like the day they do. It exists to justify keeping Article
# 4's matching carried-void and recall checks, which are subsumed today and are
# the ONLY thing standing here. If false(Tyr) below ever reads TRUE, the
# conjuncts were removed and the justification with them.
:expect-pins 5

# The route bypasses the guards: a signer voided in a prior period gets a pen,
# and so does a recalled one. Neither could hold one against the real file.
? rotten(Vex).
# => TRUE

? permits(Review, Vex).
# => TRUE

? broken(Boss).
# => TRUE

? permits(Review, Boss).
# => TRUE

# ...and the void STILL fails, because the multi-sig's own kept conjuncts
# catch what the credential rules no longer do. This is the arming case:
# against a copy with the conjuncts stripped as well, this verdict flips.
? false(Tyr).
# => FALSE
